E2 POWER UNIT MANUFACTURER OBLIGATIONS

Power Unit Manufacturer Obligations Each Power Unit Manufacturer must:

a. demonstrate its ongoing compliance with the Power Unit Cost Cap by submitting Reporting Documentation in respect of its Reporting Group to the Cost Cap Administration by the Reporting Deadline in respect of each Financial Regulations Reporting Period and by providing any further information requested from time to time by the Cost Cap Administration;

b. cooperate fully and in a timely manner with the Cost Cap Administration in the exercise of its regulatory function, including any investigation conducted by or on behalf of the Cost Cap Administration pursuant to these Financial Regulations (Power Unit Manufacturers) and/or with the Financial Regulations (F1 Teams);

c. provide any information and documentation requested by or on behalf of the Cost Cap Administration relevant to any actual, potential or suspected instance of non-compliance with these Financial Regulations (Power Unit Manufacturers) and/or with the Financial Regulations (F1 Teams) and

d. faithfully execute its obligations under these Financial Regulations (Power Unit Manufacturers) and act at all times in a spirit of Good Faith and cooperation.

